The procedure is the **SidelinkUEInformationNR** transmission (TS 38.331, clause 5.8.3.1), whose purpose is to inform the network that the UE:

a) is interested or no longer interested in receiving/transmitting NR sidelink communication;
b) is requesting assignment or release of transmission resources for NR sidelink communication;
c) is reporting QoS parameters and QoS profile(s) related to NR sidelink communication;
d) is reporting a detected sidelink radio link failure or sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure;
e) is reporting the sidelink UE capability information of the associated peer UE for unicast communication;
f) is reporting the RLC mode information of the sidelink DRB(s) received from the associated peer UE for unicast communication;
g) is reporting the sidelink DRX configuration received from the associated peer UE for unicast communication;
h) is reporting the sidelink DRX assistance information received from the associated peer UE for unicast communication;
i) is reporting (for groupcast/broadcast) [FFS additional information];
j) is reporting, for groupcast/broadcast, the Destination Layer-2 ID and QoS profile associated with interested services for which sidelink DRX is applied;
k) is reporting DRX configuration reject information from its associated peer RX UE (TX UE, resource allocation mode 1); and
l) is reporting parameters related to U2N relay operation.

